  "scope": "Post-hoc common-backend replay of the November 25 fixed-content study. The model received visible units, roles, entities, relations, action owners, preferences, a canvas and a reference width table. The rules read only fields from that projection and computed needed widths with the frozen font metrics. The model could submit any accepted Row/Column tree; the fixed rules produced a tree of that grammar without enumerating a common finite menu. Both original trees kept their submitted topology and leaf IDs through the same frozen geometry, emitter, protocol, reference geometry and static source/action checks. Identical wire bytes identify candidates for same-task screenshot reuse. This replay adds no device or independent human observations. The separate 187-case experiment used different content contracts."
